index 4479b53..2041ed6 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,43 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Reader accounts and passkeys
+
+The sign-in and sign-up pages support passwords and discoverable passkeys. After
+signing in, **My account** opens `/devtools-times/account`, where readers can add,
+rename, and remove passkeys. Each change requires a fresh passkey or password
+verification. A password-free account must keep at least one passkey; add a second
+passkey on another device or security key for recovery.
+
+This sample now uses its own same-origin account API. Accounts from the previous
+remote `times_cdn` demo API are separate and are not automatically migrated.
+Create an account here to use these flows. Passwords are salted and hashed with
+scrypt; the server never receives biometric data or private keys. Registration
+and authentication use [SimpleWebAuthn](https://simplewebauthn.dev/docs/packages/server)
+with required user verification, short-lived single-use challenges, origin and RP
+ID validation, and signature counter updates.
+
+Passkeys require HTTPS (localhost is also supported). They are scoped to the
+hostname, so use a stable hostname. Set `AUTH_ORIGIN` to your exact public origin
+(e.g. `https://news.example.com`, without a path or trailing slash) when deploying
+behind a proxy; otherwise the request origin is used.
+
+Account records are stored in `.data/accounts.json`, excluded from Git. Set
+`AUTH_DATA_FILE` to a file on a persistent volume to retain accounts across
+restarts and deploys. The JSON store, replay protection, and request limiter are
+intended for a **single Node instance**. Before a multi-instance deployment,
+replace these with shared database storage, atomic challenge/grant consumption,
+and a shared rate limiter. Astro's session storage must also persist and be
+shared across instances. There is no email recovery flow in this sample.
+
+Validation (Node 22.18+ or Node 24+):
+
+```sh
+pnpm test
+pnpm run build
+```
+
+The tests exercise password hashing, replay/expiry protection, last-method
+protection, public account serialization, and atomic account storage. They do not
+launch a server or a browser.
